, "num_reviews": 7, "playtime_forever": 11805, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4229, "last_played": 1786856586, "avatar": "377e60f519273a2884022a513e5b8118f73f9bf0"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game started my gambling addiction when I was a kid. Now as a grown man, it fuels it! 10/10 loot boxes will bang okay?", "timestamp_created": 1755097487, "timestamp_updated": 1755097487, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.571595489978790283", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": true, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "201378868", "author": {"steamid": "76561198120088653", "personaname": "neo667goelm", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198120088653/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 195, "playtime_forever": 2296, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2296, "last_played": 1754133513, "avatar": "4c555ad0eef2cb39c499d44245dc5e8a836f15ef"}, "language": "english", "review": "After playing the first two games it was time to play the most divisive one, that god the fanbase all riled up. And frankly I don't quite see why. \r\n\r\nThe game has in general the format of the previous games. A main story regarding the same intergalactic menace, Shepard and his crew going on adventures, bonding the team and making difficult choices. The same stuff is here, maybe some more toned down. The choices are there but not as often or as impactful. The rpg systems are toned down too. The orbit planets/send scaners for resources is almost scrapped and rarely used. \r\n\r\nThe game play is way better, making Mass Effect 3 more of an action game rather than a space rpg. And that's ok, as the gameplay and gunplay of the previous two games are attrocious. The stories still pack a punch, as the finale dares to make some bold choices (like the ones they don't trust you to make). But it is good, the story scenarios are good (which I won't spoil) and the ending... it's a fine ending. I don't know why it got people so riled up. \r\n\r\nAnd my main problem is, how did Mass Effect gain such a fanatic audience? They are ok as games, and good as stories, but that's that. Yes they have their moments of brilliance, but they are not \"brilliant games\". They're fun and enjoyable, but in my book very far from creating a fanbase let alone a franchise.", "timestamp_created": 1754243444, "timestamp_updated": 1754243444, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.477636426687240601", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "201302530", "author": {"steamid": "76561198962007280", "personaname": "monsef987", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/monsef987/", "num_games_owned": 581, "num_reviews": 159, "playtime_forever": 5302, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5302, "last_played": 1753976567, "avatar": "10f7ed46925c5b8407cd6431356a250eae3fc72d"}, "language": "english", "review": "Masterpiece", "timestamp_created": 1754157293, "timestamp_updated": 1754157293, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 5, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.590023934841156006", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "201294126", "author": {"steamid": "76561199007476066", "personaname": "Alexius", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/dwdj69/", "num_games_owned": 4720, "num_reviews": 1648, "playtime_forever": 22